final List<Map<String,dynamic>> a2Unit4CourseData = <Map<String,dynamic>>[
 _u4(1,"Use the present perfect to talk about experiences without saying exactly when.","I have visited Nairobi twice.","J’ai visité Nairobi deux fois.","Which sentence describes life experience?","I have visited Nairobi.",["I visit Nairobi yesterday.","I have visit Nairobi.",0],Have visited is the correct present perfect form.,undefined),
 _u4(2,"Use Have you ever + past participle to ask whether an experience happened at any time.","Have you ever ridden a horse?","As-tu déjà monté à cheval ?","Complete: Have you ever ___ sushi?","eat",["ate","eaten",2],After have, use the past participle eaten.,undefined),
 _u4(3,"Most regular verbs form the past participle with -ed.","She has finished her homework.","Elle a terminé ses devoirs.","Past participle of clean?","cleaned",["cleaning","cleans",0],Cleaned is the regular past participle.,undefined),
 _u4(4,"Some common verbs have irregular past participles that must be learned.","We have seen that film.","Nous avons vu ce film.","Past participle of write?","wrote",["written","writing",1],Written is the past participle of write.,undefined),
 _u4(5,"Use already in affirmative sentences for something completed sooner than expected; use yet in questions and negatives.","I have already eaten, but he hasn’t eaten yet.","J’ai déjà mangé, mais lui n’a pas encore mangé.","Choose the correct sentence.","I have yet finished.",["I have already finished.","I already have finish.",1],Already fits the affirmative sentence.,undefined),
 _u4(6,"Use just with the present perfect for a very recent action.","The bus has just arrived.","Le bus vient d’arriver.","The train has ___ left.","just",["yet","ever",0],Just indicates that the action happened a moment ago.,undefined),
 _u4(7,"Use never for no experience and ever mainly in questions or comparisons.","I have never flown in a plane.","Je n’ai jamais pris l’avion.","Which means « jamais » in this sentence?","never",["already","since",0],Never expresses that the experience has not happened.,undefined),
 _u4(8,"Use for with a duration and since with the starting point.","I have lived here for two years, since 2024.","J’habite ici depuis deux ans, depuis 2024.","Choose the duration phrase.","since Monday",["for three weeks","since 2022",1],For three weeks names a duration.,undefined),
 _u4(9,"Use past simple for a finished time and present perfect when the exact time is not stated or the period remains relevant.","I saw her yesterday, but I have seen her before.","Je l’ai vue hier, mais je l’ai déjà vue auparavant.","Which phrase names a finished time?","ever",["yesterday","before",1],Yesterday normally calls for the past simple.,undefined),
 _u4(10,"Ask about experiences with Have you ever + past participle.","Have you ever slept in a tent?","As-tu déjà dormi dans une tente ?","Choose the correct question.","Did you ever went camping?",["Have you ever gone camping?","Have you ever go camping?",1],Have + subject + past participle forms the question.,undefined),
 _u4(11,"Use appointment phrases to arrange a specific time with a professional.","Could I make an appointment for Friday?","Pourrais-je prendre rendez-vous pour vendredi ?","Which is a polite request?","I want appointment now.",["Could I make an appointment?","Appointment me.",1],Could I…? is a polite way to request an appointment.,undefined),
 _u4(12,"Use Could we move it to…? to change an appointment politely.","Could we move it to Monday morning?","Pourrions-nous le déplacer à lundi matin ?","You need a new time. What can you say?","Move it now.",["Could we reschedule it?","You are late.",1],Reschedule means arrange for a different time.,undefined),
 _u4(13,"Explain a problem simply and give relevant details.","I have a headache and a fever.","J’ai mal à la tête et de la fièvre.","Which phrase describes a symptom?","I have a headache.",["I have a ticket.","I have a suitcase.",0],A headache is a health symptom.,undefined),
 _u4(14,"At a pharmacy, explain what you need and ask for advice.","Could I have something for a cough?","Pourrais-je avoir quelque chose contre la toux ?","Where would you ask for cough medicine?","At a pharmacy",["At a platform","At a checkout only",0],A pharmacist can advise about suitable non-prescription remedies.,undefined),
 _u4(15,"Use have a sore throat, feel dizzy, and similar phrases for symptoms.","I feel dizzy when I stand up.","J’ai des vertiges quand je me lève.","Which phrase describes dizziness?","I feel dizzy.",["I feel hungry for a ticket.","I am platform.",0],Feel dizzy describes a symptom.,undefined),
 _u4(16,"Use should/shouldn’t to offer simple health advice.","You should drink water and rest.","Tu devrais boire de l’eau et te reposer.","Choose suitable advice for someone who is tired.","You should rest.",["You should to rest.","You should resting.",0],Should is followed by the base verb without to.,undefined),
 _u4(17,"Use should + base verb and shouldn’t + base verb.","You shouldn’t skip breakfast every day.","Tu ne devrais pas sauter le petit-déjeuner chaque jour.","Complete: You should ___ more sleep.","get",["to get","getting",0],Should is followed by get.,undefined),
 _u4(18,"Describe symptoms and answer basic questions at a medical appointment.","How long have you had the pain?","Depuis combien de temps avez-vous cette douleur ?","Which question asks about duration?","How long have you had it?",["How many pain?","Where time pain?",0],How long asks about duration.,undefined),
 _u4(19,"Follow short instructions by identifying the action and sequence.","Take this medicine with food.","Prenez ce médicament avec de la nourriture.","What does with food mean?","Before every meal only",["Together with something to eat","Without water or food",1],With food means taking it while eating or with a meal.,undefined),
 _u4(20,"Use frequency words to describe healthy habits.","I usually walk for twenty minutes.","Je marche généralement pendant vingt minutes.","Which word describes frequency?","usually",["yesterday","tomorrow",0],Usually describes how often an action happens.,undefined),
 _u4(21,"Ask about tickets, prices, and travel options.","Could I have a return ticket to the city?","Pourrais-je avoir un billet aller-retour pour la ville ?","A return ticket includes…","only the outward journey",["the outward and return journeys","a hotel room",1],A return ticket covers both directions.,undefined),
 _u4(22,"Ask station staff about departures and platforms.","Which platform does the train leave from?","De quel quai part le train ?","Where do passengers wait for a train?","On a platform",["At a pharmacy","In a fitting room",0],Passengers board trains from platforms.,undefined),
 _u4(23,"At check-in, present your passport and confirm your destination.","Here is my passport. I’m checking in for Flight 204.","Voici mon passeport. Je m’enregistre pour le vol 204.","Where do you check in for a flight?","At the airport desk",["At the hotel breakfast only","At the train platform",0],Airline check-in takes place at the airport or online.,undefined),
 _u4(24,"Ask when transport leaves and check the time carefully.","What time does the next bus depart?","À quelle heure part le prochain bus ?","Which word means « partir » for a bus?","depart",["borrow","return an item",0],Depart means to leave a place.,undefined),
 _u4(25,"Listen for platform numbers, destinations, and delays.","The train to Kolwezi is delayed by ten minutes.","Le train pour Kolwezi a dix minutes de retard.","If a train is delayed, it is…","early",["late","cancelled for certain",1],Delayed means later than scheduled.,undefined),
 _u4(26,"Ask for a room and confirm the dates and number of guests.","I’d like a double room for two nights.","Je voudrais une chambre double pour deux nuits.","A double room is usually for…","two people",["ten people","one night only",0],A double room normally has a bed for two people.,undefined),
 _u4(27,"Give your name and reservation details at reception.","I have a reservation under the name Martin.","J’ai une réservation au nom de Martin.","Where do you check into a hotel?","At reception",["At airport security","At a clothes shop",0],Hotel guests usually check in at reception.,undefined),
 _u4(28,"Report a missing towel or a problem with the room politely.","Excuse me, the shower isn’t working.","Excusez-moi, la douche ne fonctionne pas.","Which phrase politely reports a problem?","The shower isn’t working.",["Give me another room now!","You bad hotel.",0],Excuse me introduces a polite complaint.,undefined),
 _u4(29,"Ask where places are and how to get there.","Could you tell me how to get to the museum?","Pourriez-vous me dire comment aller au musée ?","Which question asks for directions politely?","Where museum you?",["Could you tell me how to get there?","You tell museum.",1],Could you tell me…? is a polite request.,undefined),
 _u4(30,"Use past simple to describe a completed trip in order.","We arrived on Friday and stayed for three nights.","Nous sommes arrivés vendredi et sommes restés trois nuits.","Which tense describes the completed journey?","past simple",["present continuous only","imperative",0],Arrived and stayed describe completed past events.,undefined),
 _u4(31,"Ask to see a different size and explain what you need.","Do you have this shirt in a larger size?","Avez-vous cette chemise dans une taille plus grande ?","What do you ask for if a shirt is too small?","A larger size",["A train platform","A prescription",0],A larger size is bigger.,undefined),
 _u4(32,"Use size words and ask whether an item is available.","Do you have these shoes in size 42?","Avez-vous ces chaussures en pointure 42 ?","Which word refers to shoe measurement?","size",["platform","appointment",0],Size identifies the measurement of clothing or shoes.,undefined),
 _u4(33,"Use try on to ask permission to test clothing before buying.","Can I try this jacket on?","Puis-je essayer cette veste ?","What does try on mean?","wear briefly to see if it fits",["return by train","pay twice",0],Try on means put on clothing to check fit or appearance.,undefined),
 _u4(34,"Ask how much something costs and compare options.","This one is cheaper, but that one is better quality.","Celui-ci est moins cher, mais l’autre est de meilleure qualité.","Which word means « moins cher »?","cheaper",["expensive","larger",0],Cheaper is the comparative of cheap.,undefined),
 _u4(35,"Explain a reason for returning a product and ask about the policy.","I’d like to return this because it’s too small.","Je voudrais retourner cet article parce qu’il est trop petit.","Why is the customer returning it?","It is too small.",["It is a train.","It is tomorrow.",0],Too small explains why the item does not fit.,undefined),
 _u4(36,"Use could I…? for polite requests in shops and services.","Could I pay by card, please?","Pourrais-je payer par carte, s’il vous plaît ?","Which is the most polite request?","Pay by card now.",["Could I pay by card, please?","I pay card you.",1],Could I… please? is polite and natural.,undefined),
 _u4(37,"Use Shall I…? to offer to do something for another person.","Shall I carry that bag for you?","Voulez-vous que je porte ce sac pour vous ?","Which phrase offers help?","Shall I carry it?",["You carry it.","I carried it yesterday.",0],Shall I…? can offer help.,undefined),
 _u4(38,"Use Let’s + base verb to suggest doing something together.","Let’s meet outside the library at five.","Retrouvons-nous devant la bibliothèque à cinq heures.","Complete: Let’s ___ a taxi.","take",["to take","taking",0],Let’s is followed by the base form take.,undefined),
 _u4(39,"Accept or decline invitations politely and give a short reason.","I’d love to, but I have to study tonight.","J’aimerais beaucoup, mais je dois étudier ce soir.","Which answer politely declines?","No. Go away.",["I’d love to, but I can’t tonight.","Invitation not.",1],The phrase shows interest and gives a reason.,undefined),
 _u4(40,"Use because to introduce a reason.","I took a taxi because it was raining.","J’ai pris un taxi parce qu’il pleuvait.","Which word introduces the reason?","because",["although","first",0],Because introduces the cause or reason.,undefined),
 _u4(41,"Use sequence words to explain steps in order.","First, buy a ticket. Then, find your platform.","D’abord, achetez un billet. Ensuite, trouvez votre quai.","Which word usually starts the sequence?","First",["Finally","Although",0],First introduces the first step.,undefined),
 _u4(42,"Use before and after to show the order of events.","Wash your hands before you eat.","Lave-toi les mains avant de manger.","What does before mean?","after",["earlier than an event","because",1],Before means earlier than another event.,undefined),
 _u4(43,"Use so to introduce a result.","The road was closed, so we took another route.","La route était fermée, alors nous avons pris un autre itinéraire.","Why did they take another route?","The road was closed.",["They bought a shirt.","They had an appointment.",0],So introduces the result of the road being closed.,undefined),
 _u4(44,"Use although to contrast two ideas.","Although it was raining, we went for a walk.","Bien qu’il pleuve, nous sommes allés nous promener.","What does although express?","contrast",["time only","ownership",0],Although introduces a contrast.,undefined),
 _u4(45,"Explain a simple process with ordered verbs.","To make tea, boil water, add tea, and wait.","Pour faire du thé, faites bouillir l’eau, ajoutez le thé et attendez.","Which verb starts the process?","boil",["return","compare",0],The example begins by boiling water.,undefined),
 _u4(46,"Give clear instructions using imperatives and polite phrases.","Please turn left after the bridge.","Tournez à gauche après le pont, s’il vous plaît.","Which sentence is a direction?","Please turn left after the bridge.",["I have turned left yesterday.","Left is very nice.",0],Turn left gives a clear instruction.,undefined),
 _u4(47,"Use have to for obligations and rules.","You have to show your ticket before boarding.","Vous devez montrer votre billet avant d’embarquer.","What does have to express?","obligation",["possibility in the past","comparison",0],Have to expresses something necessary.,undefined),
 _u4(48,"Use can to ask for or express permission in everyday situations.","Can I sit here?","Puis-je m’asseoir ici ?","Which question asks permission?","Can I sit here?",["I can yesterday sit.","Do I sat here?",0],Can I…? is a common permission question.,undefined),
 _u4(49,"Review everyday language in a short service interaction.","Could I book a room, and what time is breakfast?","Pourrais-je réserver une chambre et à quelle heure est le petit-déjeuner ?","Which phrase is a polite request?","Could I book a room?",["Book room me.","I booking yesterday.",0],Could I…? makes the request polite.,undefined),
 _u4(50,"Combine experience, travel, requests, and explanations in a short exchange.","I’ve never flown before, so I’m asking for help at check-in.","Je n’ai jamais pris l’avion, alors je demande de l’aide à l’enregistrement.","What does the speaker need?","help at check-in",["a new shirt size","a pharmacy appointment",0],The sentence explicitly says the speaker is asking for check-in help.,undefined),
